      <div class="content-block">
        <h2>Reading the <span class="text-green">Tables</span></h2>
        <p><strong>NTR R1:</strong> one adjuster, changing compression and rebound damping together. Supplied with Nitron race springs and top mounts.</p>
        <p><strong>NTR R3:</strong> three-way kits with a reservoir, piggyback or on a hose as shown. High-speed compression, low-speed compression and rebound are each adjusted separately.</p>
        <p><strong>NTR RoadSport:</strong> one adjuster, changing compression and rebound damping together. RoadSport kits use form springs and the car's original top mounts.</p>
        <p><strong>elec-TRON:</strong> Nitron's electronically controlled damper kits. See <a href="/nitron-electron/">Nitron elec-TRON</a> for how the system works and what it needs on the car.</p>
        <p><strong>FAL:</strong> front axle lift. Nitron's standalone system raises the front by 25mm at the damper, and the kit contains the cylinders, hydraulic lines, pump, wiring loom and controller.</p>
        <p><strong>Coil-over and divorced:</strong> where a car can be fitted with the rear spring on the damper (coil-over) or in its original separate position (divorced), Nitron lists a rear rate for each.</p>
        <p><strong>FR and TD:</strong> Nitron's Fast Road and Track Day spring specifications. The kit is supplied with one of these unless different rates are specified for your car.</p>
      </div>

